# opt-njmp-last: njmp=4 and then nout=2 on a later @ line, which one wins (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: rows=5
# pc: ok
# ruling: matches: nout and njmp set one value, so the last entry wins; here nout=2 (crates/pc-ode/docs/language.md, Lists)
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=4,dt=0.5,meth=euler,njmp=4
@ nout=2
